1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--reading-doesn-t-mean-books","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/reading-doesn-t-mean-books","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/reading-doesn-t-mean-books","sourceHash":"5731ed77cb413c2d5e409167d805c26990c5c5fa0727c9a0287ffadc4b2cd9a9","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:00.731Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Reading Doesn't Mean Books","zh":"阅读不等于读书"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When the Refold roadmap says \"reading,\" it doesn't mean sitting down with a novel. Reading means engaging with any text in the target language — and at the beginning of your journey, the best reading you can do is watching TV with subtitles.","zh":"Refold 路线图中所说的“阅读”，并不意味着坐下来读一本小说。阅读是指接触目标语言中的任何文本——而在学习旅程的初期，你能进行的最佳阅读活动就是看带字幕的电视节目。"}},{"id":"what-counts-as-reading","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What Counts as Reading","zh":"哪些活动算阅读"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"TV shows with target-language subtitles","zh":"观看带目标语言字幕的电视节目"},{"en":"YouTube videos with subtitles","zh":"观看带字幕的 YouTube 视频"},{"en":"Manga, comics, webtoons","zh":"漫画、连环画和网络漫画"},{"en":"Social media posts and comments","zh":"社交媒体帖子和评论"},{"en":"News articles and blog posts","zh":"新闻文章和博客文章"},{"en":"Text messages and chat","zh":"短信和聊天消息"},{"en":"Graded readers and novels","zh":"分级读物和小说"},{"en":"Subtitled podcasts or audiobooks with transcripts","zh":"带字幕的播客，或配有文字稿的有声书"}]},{"id":"tv-is-sometimes-better-than-books","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"TV Is (Sometimes) Better Than Books","zh":"电视节目（有时）比书籍更好"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"In the early phases, TV with subtitles is superior to books for most learners because:","zh":"在早期阶段，对大多数学习者而言，观看带字幕的电视节目比读书更有效，原因如下："}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"You get three input channels (visual context + text + audio)","zh":"你可以同时获得三个输入渠道（视觉语境＋文字＋音频）"},{"en":"The visual context helps you understand without looking things up","zh":"视觉语境能帮助你理解内容，减少查词需求"},{"en":"The audio trains your ear simultaneously","zh":"音频可以同时训练听辨能力"},{"en":"Content is more engaging for most people than graded readers","zh":"对大多数人来说，这类内容比分级读物更有吸引力"},{"en":"Episodes are short enough to maintain focus","zh":"每集时间够短，容易保持专注"}]},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Books become more valuable later (Phase 3 onward) when your vocabulary is large enough to read comfortably, and especially useful in Phases 5+ when extensive reading is the best way to expand vocabulary beyond everyday words.","zh":"到了后期（阶段 3 及以后），当你的词汇量足以支持舒适阅读时，书籍会变得更有价值；尤其是在阶段 5 及以后，广泛阅读是将词汇量拓展到日常用词之外的最佳方式。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Don't feel bad if you're not \"reading books\" yet. If you're watching TV with subtitles, you're reading — and it's probably the most effective form of reading for your current level.","zh":"如果你还没有开始“读书”，不必感到沮丧。只要你在观看带字幕的电视节目，你就是在阅读——而且这很可能是对你当前水平最有效的阅读形式。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
